### cloud-save-service — collection HTTP
#
# Requer a stack no ar:
#   docker compose -f infra/docker/docker-compose.yml up
#
# Endpoints de jogador exigem JWT do identity (ADR-0009) + header X-Game-Id
# (multi-tenant por jogo, ADR-0017). O login captura o token.
# GoLand/IntelliJ: clique no ▶. (VS Code REST Client: ver nota no fim.)
#
# Acompanhe: Grafana http://localhost:3000 e o console do MinIO
# http://localhost:9001 (minioadmin/minioadmin), bucket cloud-save
# (keys ficam como {gameID}/{playerID}).

@identityHost = http://localhost:8081
@cloudSaveHost = http://localhost:8084
@handle = Save_1
@password = supersecret

# Jogo no header X-Game-Id. "sandbox" = jogo default da migração (UUID nil).
@gameId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### (uma vez) Criar a conta no identity
POST {{identityHost}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "{{handle}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Login no identity -> captura o token
# @name login
POST {{identityHost}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "{{handle}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Salvar o save (blob — aqui um JSON, mas o serviço trata como opaco)
PUT {{cloudSaveHost}}/me/save
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Game-Id: {{gameId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "level": 7, "hp": 50, "inventory": ["sword", "shield"] }

### Carregar o save (volta no mesmo Content-Type)
GET {{cloudSaveHost}}/me/save
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Game-Id: {{gameId}}

### Sobrescrever (last-write-wins)
PUT {{cloudSaveHost}}/me/save
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Game-Id: {{gameId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "level": 8, "hp": 100 }

### Sem X-Game-Id -> 400 missing_game
GET {{cloudSaveHost}}/me/save
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Admin (control plane INTERNO) ---
# Exige o header X-Internal-Key (ADR-0018), NÃO o JWT. Devolve metadados +
# blob em base64. Alimenta a aba Cloud saves do painel.
@internalKey = dev-internal-key

### Save do jogador {playerID} no jogo {gameId} (404 se não houver)
GET {{cloudSaveHost}}/admin/games/{{gameId}}/players/guest-123/save
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Sem a internal key -> 401
GET {{cloudSaveHost}}/admin/games/{{gameId}}/players/guest-123/save

# --- VS Code REST Client ---
# O bloco "> {% ... %}" é sintaxe do JetBrains. No REST Client, remova-o e use
# Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
